## 13. Cloud Computing

Cloud computing provides on-demand access to compute, storage, networking, databases, and other services.

Major providers include:

- Microsoft Azure
- Amazon Web Services (AWS)
- Google Cloud Platform (GCP)

### Benefits

- Elastic scaling
- Faster provisioning
- Managed services
- Reduced need to purchase all physical infrastructure
- Usage-based pricing models

Cloud is not automatically cheaper or secure by default.

Costs may include compute, storage, data transfer, managed services, transactions, and idle resources.

Security follows a shared-responsibility model. The provider and customer have different responsibilities depending on the service.

### Learn One Cloud First

Learning one provider deeply can help establish transferable knowledge about:

- Object storage
- Identity and access
- Compute
- Networking
- Orchestration
- Monitoring
- Security
- Governance
- Cost management

Examples of cloud object storage include ADLS Gen2, Amazon S3, and Google Cloud Storage.

Free credits and trial terms change over time, so current offers should be checked in official provider documentation.

