## 15. Azure Data Engineering Services

### Azure Event Hubs

A managed service for high-volume event ingestion and streaming data.

### Azure SQL Database

A managed relational database service on Azure.

Its capabilities and operational behavior are not identical to every SQL Server deployment or relational platform.

### Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2

ADLS Gen2 provides data-lake storage capabilities on Azure Blob Storage with hierarchical namespace support.

It is commonly used to store analytical files and lakehouse data.

### Azure Data Factory

ADF provides data integration and orchestration capabilities, including connectors, copy activities, scheduling, and pipeline coordination.

It can invoke other compute services to perform transformations.

### Azure Databricks

A managed data and AI platform commonly used for Spark-based distributed transformations and lakehouse workloads.

### Azure Synapse Analytics

An Azure analytics service that provides SQL and other analytical capabilities depending on the component used.

It can be part of an analytical or warehouse architecture.

### Power BI

Power BI is used to build:

- Reports
- Dashboards
- Semantic models
- KPIs
- Interactive business visualizations

