## 17. End-to-End Azure Data Engineering Architecture

A possible architecture is:

1. Data originates from databases, APIs, files, IoT devices, or applications.
2. Azure Event Hubs receives streaming events where required.
3. Azure Data Factory coordinates batch ingestion and data movement.
4. ADLS Gen2 stores raw or minimally changed data in Bronze.
5. Databricks/Spark cleans and transforms data into Silver.
6. Curated transformations create Gold tables and business models.
7. Power BI, SQL analytics, or data-science tools consume appropriate curated datasets.
8. Governance, identity, monitoring, deployment, and cost management operate across the platform.

### Architecture Diagram

```text
Operational Databases / APIs / Files / IoT
                    |
          +---------+---------+
          |                   |
      Batch Data          Event Streams
          |                   |
  Azure Data Factory    Azure Event Hubs
          |                   |
          +---------+---------+
                    |
            ADLS Gen2 — Bronze
                    |
          Azure Databricks / Spark
                    |
            ADLS Gen2 — Silver
                    |
         Curated Transformations
                    |
             Gold Data Models
                    |
          +---------+---------+
          |                   |
       Power BI         SQL / Data Science
          |
    Reports and KPIs
```

### Important Design Note

Not every solution needs every service.

A batch-only pipeline may not need Event Hubs. A lakehouse may serve some consumers without a separate Synapse layer. Service selection should follow requirements rather than a fixed diagram.

