## 18. Data Engineering Best Practices

### Data Quality

Validate completeness, uniqueness, validity, consistency, and freshness.

### Reliability

Design for failures, retries, recovery, and safe publication of results.

### Idempotency

Ensure that retries do not create incorrect duplicate effects.

### Incremental Processing

Avoid unnecessary full reloads when reliable change tracking is available.

### Security

Use least-privilege access, secure credentials, appropriate identity management, and clear data-access policies.

### Observability

Track pipeline status, runtime, row counts, data freshness, rejected records, and quality metrics.

### Governance

Maintain clear ownership, discoverable metadata, lineage, and appropriate retention rules.

### CI/CD

Use source control, automated tests, and controlled deployments across development, testing, and production.

### Cost Management

Monitor resource usage, eliminate unnecessary compute, review data movement, and measure performance-cost trade-offs.

### Documentation

Document assumptions, architecture decisions, data contracts, quality expectations, and operational recovery procedures.

