## 19. Interview Preparation Checklist

### Fundamentals

- Explain the Data Engineering lifecycle.
- Distinguish upstream and downstream systems.
- Explain relational databases, SQL, and NoSQL.
- Compare full and incremental loads.
- Explain CDC, watermarks, and idempotency.

### Data Modeling

- Define fact-table grain.
- Distinguish facts and dimensions.
- Explain star and snowflake schemas.
- Explain SCD Types 0, 1, 2, and 3.
- Describe surrogate keys and effective dates.

### Storage and Processing

- Compare data lakes, warehouses, and lakehouses.
- Compare CSV, Avro, Parquet, and ORC.
- Explain Delta Lake, ACID, time travel, and schema evolution.
- Explain Spark drivers, executors, shuffles, partitions, and skew.
- Distinguish processing from orchestration.

### Azure

- Explain Event Hubs, Data Factory, ADLS Gen2, Databricks, Synapse, and Power BI.
- Explain Purview, Key Vault, Entra ID, Monitor, DevOps, and Cost Management.
- Draw an end-to-end architecture.
- Justify service selection and discuss trade-offs.

### Scenario-Based Preparation

- Handle duplicate records after pipeline retries.
- Troubleshoot a slow Spark job.
- Design an incremental load for a large dataset.
- Preserve historical dimension changes.
- Handle unexpected schema changes.
- Improve data freshness.
- Reduce cloud costs.
- Secure pipeline credentials.
- Monitor failures and data quality.
- Prevent incomplete data from reaching consumers.

