## Final Takeaways

1. Data Engineering focuses on reliable and maintainable data delivery.
2. Ingestion strategy should reflect business latency and correctness requirements.
3. Define the grain of a fact table before designing its schema.
4. Choose SCD types according to historical reporting needs.
5. Select file formats based on workload characteristics.
6. Delta Lake adds table-management capabilities beyond a collection of plain files.
7. Spark distributes processing, while orchestration tools coordinate workflows.
8. Bronze, Silver, and Gold represent increasing data refinement.
9. Azure services often complement each other rather than acting as direct replacements.
10. Production data platforms require quality, reliability, security, governance, observability, deployment discipline, and cost management.

